character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  蔬 | shū | vegetable; greens; coarse food | verdura; hortaliza; comida frugal | 艹 | grass / plant | 艹 (herbs, garden greens) | 疏 (shū, dredge / disperse / phonetic) | 14 | 上下结构 | Phono-semantic compound: grass radical 艹 denoting edible garden crops, paired with 疏 (dredge/open channels for water flow). | Green leafy herbs (艹) nurtured in well-dredged, irrigated garden soil (疏) yield fresh vegetables (蔬). | Brotes de hierba tierna (艹) regados por acequias limpias (疏) crecen lozanos dando ricas verduras (蔬). | 55 | TNLI | 
  菜 | cài | vegetable; dish; cuisine; food course | verdura; plato; comida; guiso | 艹 | grass / plant | 艹 (plant, herbs) | 采 (cǎi, hand plucking fruit/leaves) | 11 | 上下结构 | Ancient pictogram showing an active hand 爫 plucking edible herb leaves and berries 艹 from plants 木. | Hands pluck (采) fresh edible tender leaves and greens from the garden soil (艹) to prepare a savory dish (菜). | Una mano recolecta con primor (采) brotes comestibles de la mata (艹) para aderezar un plato sano (菜). | 51 | TBD | 

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Well-dredged leafy herbs (蔬) plucked fresh from the garden patch (菜) provide nourishing household vegetables (蔬菜).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Hortalizas bien regadas (蔬) cosechadas frescas del huerto (菜) forman las verduras cotidianas (蔬菜).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In ancient Chinese culinary classification, 蔬 (wild and garden edible herbs) stood alongside 谷 (grains), 果 (fruits), and 畜 (livestock). Consuming 蔬食 (simple vegetable fare) was an esteemed Daoist and Buddhist sign of ascetic purity, detachment from slaughter, and spiritual clarity.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: High level 1st tone followed by falling 4th tone: 'shū cài' (55-51). Pronounce 'shū' with level high pitch before a firm descending drop on 'cài'.

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[5]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    疏 | shū | sparse; dredge; distant | Lacks the grass radical 艹 at the top
    梳 | shū | comb; tease hair | Has wood radical 木 on the left instead of 艹
    采 | cǎi | pluck; gather; color | Lacks the grass radical 艹 at the top
    彩 | cǎi | color; applause; lottery | Has three bristle slashes 彡 on the right of 采
    踩 | cǎi | step on; tread | Has foot radical 足 on the left of 采
  etymological_cognates[5]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
